{% doc %}
  Renders global Organization and WebSite structured data for NUR Fragrances.
{% enddoc %}

{% capture nur_search_target %}{{ shop.url }}{{ routes.search_url }}?q={search_term_string}{% endcapture %}
{%- liquid
  assign instagram_url = blank
  if settings.social_instagram != blank
    if settings.social_instagram contains 'http'
      assign instagram_url = settings.social_instagram
    else
      assign instagram_handle = settings.social_instagram | remove: '@'
      assign instagram_url = 'https://www.instagram.com/' | append: instagram_handle
    endif
  endif
  assign tiktok_url = blank
  if settings.social_tiktok != blank
    if settings.social_tiktok contains 'http'
      assign tiktok_url = settings.social_tiktok
    else
      assign tiktok_handle = settings.social_tiktok | remove: '@'
      assign tiktok_url = 'https://www.tiktok.com/@' | append: tiktok_handle
    endif
  endif
-%}

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  {%- comment -%}
    OnlineStore, not Organization and not LocalBusiness. NUR sells and ships
    online with no premises the public can walk into, so Store/LocalBusiness
    with openingHours would assert a shopfront that does not exist. OnlineStore
    is a schema.org subtype of Organization, so every node already pointing at
    #organization keeps resolving unchanged.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  "@type": "OnlineStore",
  "@id": {{ shop.url | append: '#organization' | json }},
  "name": "NUR Fragrance",
  "alternateName": "NUR Fragrances",
  "url": {{ shop.url | json }},
  "description": "NUR Fragrance is a Germany-based online shop for Arabian perfume samples, decants and discovery sets, helping customers test fragrances before purchasing a full bottle.",
  "logo": {{ 'favicon-nur-logo.svg' | asset_url | prepend: 'https:' | json }},
  "email": "info@nur-fragrance.com",
  {%- comment -%}
    Locality, region and country only - no streetAddress, no postalCode.

    The full postal address is published on /pages/impressum and
    /pages/widerrufsrecht because section 5 DDG requires it of a German shop.
    That is a legal disclosure on a legal page. It is not something to broadcast
    into the structured data of every page on the site. City level is a genuine
    local-relevance signal by itself, and it is the level this business actually
    operates at. Owner asked for Berlin only on 2026-09-14; honour that.

    Deliberately absent, and not to be added without a real source:
    - telephone - the only number NUR publishes is a personal mobile on a legal
      page. Owner's call, and the answer so far is no.
    - aggregateRating / review - NUR has no reviews at all. One invented rating
      would discredit every other claim in this graph.
    - foundingDate, numberOfEmployees, vatID - no source of truth exists.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  "address": {
    "@type": "PostalAddress",
    "addressLocality": "Berlin",
    "addressRegion": "Berlin",
    "addressCountry": "DE"
  },
  {%- comment -%}
    de-DE for the German storefront, but plain "en" for the English one. The
    English version serves the EU and fourteen international markets including
    the US, GB and AU, so regionalising it to en-DE would be a worse signal than
    leaving it unregionalised. This is a decision, not an oversight.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  "inLanguage": ["de-DE", "en"],
  "sameAs": [{% if instagram_url != blank %}{{ instagram_url | json }}{% endif %}{% if instagram_url != blank and tiktok_url != blank %},{% endif %}{% if tiktok_url != blank %}{{ tiktok_url | json }}{% endif %}],
  "contactPoint": {
    "@type": "ContactPoint",
    "contactType": "customer support",
    "email": "info@nur-fragrance.com",
    "areaServed": ["DE", "AT", "CH", "NL", "BE", "FR", "IT", "ES", "EU"],
    "availableLanguage": ["English", "German"]
  }
}
</script>

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebSite",
  "@id": {{ shop.url | append: '#website' | json }},
  "name": "NUR Fragrance",
  "url": {{ shop.url | json }},
  "publisher": {
    "@id": {{ shop.url | append: '#organization' | json }}
  },
  "inLanguage": ["de-DE", "en"],
  "potentialAction": {
    "@type": "SearchAction",
    "target": {{ nur_search_target | strip | json }},
    "query-input": "required name=search_term_string"
  }
}
</script>
